{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a quiz generator. Given a topic and difficulty, generate exactly the requested number of multiple choice questions as valid JSON. Each question has 4 options, one correct answer, and a one-sentence explanation."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Generate 4 MCQs on: Neural Networks, difficulty: beginner"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"topic\": \"Neural Networks\", \"difficulty\": \"beginner\", \"questions\": [{\"question\": \"What does dropout do during training?\", \"options\": [\"Increases the learning rate\", \"Randomly deactivates neurons to prevent overfitting\", \"Removes the bias term\", \"Adds more layers\"], \"answer\": \"Randomly deactivates neurons to prevent overfitting\", \"explanation\": \"Dropout prevents co-adaptation of neurons, improving generalization.\"}, {\"question\": \"What is backpropagation?\", \"options\": [\"A way to initialize weights\", \"An algorithm to compute gradients of the loss with respect to weights via the chain rule\", \"A type of activation function\", \"A data augmentation technique\"], \"answer\": \"An algorithm to compute gradients of the loss with respect to weights via the chain rule\", \"explanation\": \"Backpropagation applies the chain rule to efficiently compute gradients layer by layer for gradient descent updates.\"}, {\"question\": \"Which optimizer combines momentum and adaptive learning rates?\", \"options\": [\"SGD\", \"Adam\", \"Batch Gradient Descent\", \"Newton's Method\"], \"answer\": \"Adam\", \"explanation\": \"Adam maintains per-parameter adaptive learning rates using estimates of first and second moment of the gradients.\"}, {\"question\": \"What is the primary purpose of an activation function?\", \"options\": [\"To initialize weights\", \"To introduce non-linearity so the network can learn complex patterns\", \"To reduce the number of layers\", \"To normalize input data\"], \"answer\": \"To introduce non-linearity so the network can learn complex patterns\", \"explanation\": \"Without non-linear activations, a network collapses into a single linear transformation regardless of depth.\"}]}"}]}


